  - m_Id: 17117632292986885
    m_Localized: If Karma is at maximum at the start of the turn, 1 HP is restored
      to allies whose HP is lower than maximum HP.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986888
    m_Localized: '30% chance of success

      Success: Awakening 1 selected Memory

      Fail:
      Destroy the selected Memory.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986895
    m_Localized: Old boxes and unidentifiable ritual tools are lying around. There
      are still clear traces of consciousness.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986896
    m_Localized: 'dice decision

      The higher it is, the higher the Max HP increase.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986897
    m_Localized: '90% chance of success

      Success: Awakening 1 selected Memory

      Fail:
      Destroy the selected Memory.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986898
    m_Localized: 'When combat begins, mutants first schedule their actions into slots.

      The
      actions scheduled by a mutant are displayed in the timeline at the bottom.

      Only
      one variant can be scheduled for action in a slot.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986899
    m_Localized: 'By selecting a variant or selecting a reserved action

      You
      can check the information on the byeonche.

      Check the damage amount,
      effect, and range in advance.

      Predict how mutants will attack.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986900
    m_Localized: 'Actions scheduled by characters and mutants are executed in the
      order shown in the timeline.

      When all scheduled actions are performed,
      it moves on to the next turn.

      Again, you can check the mutant''s actions
      and schedule your character''s actions.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986901
    m_Localized: 'Memory is broadly divided into two types depending on how it is
      used.

      The range containing is displayed based on the direction the character
      is facing,

      It is registered directly in the slot without having to select
      a separate grid.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986902
    m_Localized: 'The range not included is within the range displayed on the battlefield.

      You
      must select a location to register for your action to be registered.

      Register
      your character''s actions so you can respond to the mutant''s actions.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986906
    m_Localized: 'Deliver a powerful slash to the target

      Deals 7 damage and
      pushes you back 1 space.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986912
    m_Localized: '================================


      Thank you for playing
      the demo version.


      What is implemented in the current version


      -
      Map creation

      - Character organization

      - Battle system

      -
      Monster AI

      - Skills and status abnormalities

      - Turn reservation
      system


      Boss battles and late-game content

      Development is in
      progress.


      ================================'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17117632292986914
    m_Localized: '1. Select one of five slots.

      2. Click on a character or
      HUD to open the character''s skill list.

      3. After selecting the movement
      skill, additionally select the grid to move to.

      4. Attack and buff skills
      are automatically registered in the direction of progress.

      3. Use your
      resources to register skills and end the turn.



      - By hovering the mouse
      over the timeline, you can see information about the action target and progress.

      -
      You can cancel registration by clicking on the registered skill on the timeline.

      -
      You can click on the monster to check its HUD and buffs/debuffs.

      - You
      can check buffs/debuffs by hovering over the icon on the character HUD.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
